{"base":"7feb0188ec550135e70f4f16a4ab7051095077b2","description":"- drop Release::author: authorship of the release COB was\n  incidental and shouldn't gate contributions; per-artifact\n  attribution stays on Artifact::author\n- replace find_delegate_release with find_or_create_by_oid in\n  the add path: a non-delegate was previously creating a new\n  release even when a delegate release already existed, causing\n  duplicate releases per commit and breaking the interactive\n  fetch picker with \"multiple delegate releases found\"\n- switch location_add to find_unique_by_oid to match the rest of\n  the write paths\n- make fetch and serve CID-centric: union locations across every\n  release containing the CID so duplicate release COBs for one\n  OID, or the same artifact reused across commits, don't leave\n  retrieval blind to known sources\n- add Releases::find_all_by_cid for the above aggregation\n- dedupe the interactive picker by commit OID: when multiple\n  release COBs exist for one commit (e.g. concurrent creation\n  across unsynced nodes), merge their artifacts into one entry\n- reinterpret list --delegates-only as \"releases containing at\n  least one delegate-authored artifact\" since releases no longer\n  have a creator DID\n- drop release-level author from display output: pretty header\n  loses \"by {author}\"; --json output no longer includes author\n  or author_alias at the release level (breaking shape change,\n  no downstream contract in-repo)\n- simplify redaction trust set to {artifact author, delegates}\n- note in README that fully deterministic COB IDs per OID would\n  require upstream changes to radicle-cob (expose commit metadata\n  on Transaction::initial) and are tracked as a follow-up","oid":"df344a42fc342e4d9f22fb457965a49128401bef","type":"revision"}